# Requests to try the API from Visual Studio / Rider (or the VS Code REST Client).
# 1. Run the "https" profile.  2. Send "Sign in" and copy accessToken into @token below.

@host = https://localhost:7211
@token = paste-the-access-token-here

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Website: projects (all, or ?category=Featured / Engineering)
GET {{host}}/api/projects

### Website: one project by its web address
GET {{host}}/api/projects/rccg-hope-house

### Website: research
GET {{host}}/api/publications

###
GET {{host}}/api/presentations

### Website: experience and skills
GET {{host}}/api/experience

###
GET {{host}}/api/skills

### Website: Contact form
POST {{host}}/api/contact/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Visitor",
  "email": "visitor@example.com",
  "organisation": "Example University",
  "topic": "Research",
  "message": "Hello! I'd like to talk about your Med-CTX paper."
}

### Sign in (use SeedData:AdminEmail and the password from User Secrets)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "enobong.adahada@gmail.com",
  "password": "your-password"
}

### Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: dashboard numbers
GET {{host}}/api/admin/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: every project, drafts included
GET {{host}}/api/admin/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: new project (as a draft)
POST {{host}}/api/admin/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Zayun API",
  "subtitle": "Portfolio Content Platform",
  "description": "The ASP.NET Core API behind zayun.net.",
  "category": "Engineering",
  "label": "Full-Stack Engineering",
  "githubUrl": "https://github.com/adahadapato/zayun-web",
  "isPrivateRepo": false,
  "tags": ["ASP.NET Core", "Clean Architecture", "CQRS"],
  "isPublished": false
}

### Admin: inbox
GET {{host}}/api/admin/contact-messages?status=New
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
